      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hmmm... Let's think this through... Teleports seem to work (in general), so it's important to identify what's different in your script.\n\nHow about trying a simplified example? I haven't tried this in-game, but here's how I usually do per-update player teleportation movement:\n\n```\n\nprivate void Update()\n\n{\n\n    var lp = Networking.LocalPlayer;\n\n    lp.TeleportTo(transform.position,\n\n                  lp.GetTrackingDataVRCPlayerApi.TrackingDataType.Origin).rotation,\n\n                  VRC_SceneDescriptor.SpawnOrientation.AlignRoomWithSpawnPoint,\n\n                  true);\n\n}\n\n```\n\nI'm not sure why you're experiencing teleportation issues, but I hope this narrows it down somewhat.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
