  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "This function appears to be incorrectly changing the rotation of the player in a seemingly uncontrollable way.\n\nI am trying to teleport a player without rotating them, so I am plugging in the player's rotation into the rotation destination.\n\nThis works whenever the player's Y rotation is positive - the player retains the same rotation.\n\nHowever, if the player's Y rotation is negative, TeleportTo seems to change that rotation to either 0, 0 ,0 or to whatever the last positive Y rotation they were was.\n\nIt being reset to 0 just seems to be random.\n\nIt didn't matter what I set teleportOrientation to. At first I wasn't using it, and it was broken. Default is broken. AlignPlayerWithSpawnPoint I believe is just the Default. And AlignRoomWithSpawnPoint sets them to 0, 0 ,0 every time ignoring the teleportRot I input.\n\nThe lerpOnRemote setting did not affect this behavior.\n\nIn the upper right of this video, you can see the Y rotation of the player as I move along a square plane.\n\nThe intended effect is that the player is being wrapped around an infinite loop. The teleport position seems to be working fine.\n\nhttps://youtu.be/qSmhU_a7Hv8\n\nI have also tried\n\nNetworking.LocalPlayer.GetTrackingData(VRCPlayerApi.TrackingDataType.AvatarRoot).rotation;\n\nBut AvatarRoot and Origin both seem to just return 0,0,0 rotations.",
